{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"3c70d4b9-41ac-4d77-aed0-c64ca759546a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The issue was caused by the **`similarity`** function returning a `float`, which DynamoDB does not accept. The first publish succeeded because the table was empty, so the `similar` list (which holds the scores) was empty and no float was written. On the second publish a score was generated, the float was sent to DynamoDB, and the operation failed with a 500 error.\n\n**Fix applied**\n- Updated `src/app.py` → **`similarity` now returns a `Decimal`** (compatible with DynamoDB) instead of a float. The conversion is done with `Decimal(str(round(...)))` to preserve precision without using a float internally.\n\n**Details and rationale** are documented in the generated artifact:\n\n[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/3c70d4b9-41ac-4d77-aed0-c64ca759546a/ANSWER.md)\n\nIt explains the root cause, the code change, which parts of the colleague’s note were useful, and next steps (e.g., adding an integration test that publishes two stories in a row).\n","duration_seconds":26.555032,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":11585,"output_tokens":2298,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":40064,"total_tokens":13883}}}
